    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0852" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg770"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 669.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 3, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit for your information a copy of a
                    private note of the 23d ultimo from M. de Geofroy; of my reply of the 30th
                    ultimo, and of a letter addressed by me to Major General Canby on the 30th
                    ultimo, in regard to the alleged entrance of the Mexican General Cortinas, with
                    an armed force, into the territory of the United States, with an assumption of
                    military authority.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>For enclosures see correspondence with the French legation.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d673-a1.xml" xpointer="d673-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
